  "img": "systems/pf1/icons/skills/light_01.jpg",
  "name": "Paladin",
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p><em>Paladins are righteous guardians of the weak. Trained under the royal banner of Ul'dah, and known by some as the Sultansworn, these paladins use the divine light inside them to protect their Oaths and their allies. Using their Divine arts to protect or heal their allies and using their Holy brand to vanquish their foes. The paladin stands as a shining bastion against encroaching darkness, a tireless champion who merges unwavering martial prowess with the sacred arts of White Magic. Clad in gleaming plate armor, they are often found on the front lines, shrugging off blows and drawing enemy aggression, while their knightswords or mighty greatswords hum with divine energy. Unlike the more focused White Mage, the paladin's spells are geared towards battlefield utility and personal enhancement: protective wards like Protect and Shell, restorative bursts of Cure or Cura, and blinding flashes of Holy magic to smite their foes. Their signature ability, akin to a Holy Strike, allows them to infuse their attacks with a burst of holy damage, often fueled by their Aether or MP pool, making them particularly devastating against fiends and the corrupted.</em></p><h2>Role</h2><p>The paladin serves as far more than just a heavily armored warrior; they are the party's unwavering bastion of righteousness and a vital cornerstone of defense and support. Their primary role lies in being a stalwart front-line combatant, capable of absorbing significant damage while dishing out holy wrath against foes, often empowered by their divine connection to the Light. Beyond pure combat, a paladin is a crucial protector, utilizing sacred magic to heal allies, cleanse negative statuses, and bestow powerful protective auras, making them a hybrid defender and white magic support. Furthermore, they act as the group's moral compass and a beacon of hope, embodying justice and chivalry, often leading the charge against encroaching darkness and ensuring the party remains true to its noblest ideals.</p><h2>Alignment</h2><p>Any non-evil alignment, most paladins tend to gravitate to good.</p><h2>Class Skills</h2><p>The paladin's class skills are Craft (Int), Diplomacy (Cha), Handle Animal (Cha), Heal (Wis), Intimidate (Cha), Knowledge (nobility) (Int), Knowledge (religion) (Int), Profession (Wis), Ride (Dex), Sense Motive (Wis), and Spellcraft (Int).</p><h2>Weapon and Armor Proficiency</h2><p>Paladins are proficient with all simple, martial weapons, and knight swords and with all armor (light, medium, and heavy) and shields (including tower shields).</p><h2>Main Ability Score</h2><p>The paladin mainly focuses on STR for martial combat and CHA for their class features.</p><h2>Code of Conduct</h2><p>A paladin must be of non-evil alignment and cannot level further into this class if she ever shifts to an evil alignment.</p>",
      "instructions": ""
    },
